+In this fork, each eligible historical occurrence contributes once to the continuation statistics, including newly completed occurrences after a cached lookup position. The selected continuation supplies both the emitted tokens and their acceptance feedback. A zero-acceptance result suppresses that continuation until the map is rebuilt; it is not counted as a generated draft on subsequent empty lookups.
+
+K4V maps are host-side acceleration state and are rebuilt at the beginning of a generation. This discards indices and acceptance feedback from a previous or replaced history, including equal-length prompt changes. Draft counts can therefore differ from an uninterrupted generation after a reset. The adaptive DFlash2 arena supports this map as an optional first proposal source for the admitted Qwen pairing, with independent DFlash/K4V maxima of 1-7 and target verification through eight rows. Set K4V M explicitly to at most seven; the native default M=48 is outside that contract. See the [K7 support and sizing guide](development/dflash2-k4v.md) for the mixed invocation, inherited cache types, reset behavior and qualification limits. The native example below retains its separate non-streaming limits.
